{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner: decisions for hugh from the simplification, cost and security review (request 55563589). Each is a product or operating choice the review cannot make. (D1) Public founding. Today anyone can found a room with no credential and no limit, and each room costs recurring money and account capacity. Options: operator-signed grant for every founding; a per-address quota with a Rate Limiting binding; proof of work; or keep it open and accept the exposure for the contest period only. The founding-gate request waits on this. (D2) Check attestation. A required tests or types check runs the proposal's own package.json scripts and lockfile, which are not under .artroom/** and so need no admin approval; a proposer can meet the obligation by changing the test script. Options: checker configuration under .artroom pins the command; an admin-approval obligation when package.json or the lockfile change; or accept that human review of the diff is the barrier, and say so in docs/policy-pack.md. (D3) Re-running checks when main moves. Every landing resets every open preview and re-runs every check (core.ts:1258-1304), so cost grows with landings times open proposals times checkers, and the LLM check never carries. Options: keep strict freshness (R-PROP-7); re-run lazily at the next land or attention; debounce. (D4) Lane fork retention. Forks are never deleted, and Artifacts storage is billed at $0.50 per GB-month from 2026-10-14; whether a fork is billed as a full copy is not documented. Options: delete after landing plus a retention period; keep forever for audit; keep until the lane's objects are pinned in the canonical repository, which they already are at propose. (D5) Legacy migrations and harness Workers. Room migrations v2 to v8, the legacy lease and ws_legacy paths, the registry legacy flag and the snapshot revision-3 upgrade exist only for states the spike deployment had before 2026-10-01 22:55; the lane B and lane G harness Workers are a third deployable topology beside spike and production. Options: wipe the spike Durable Objects, fold the migrations into one base schema and retire the harnesses to measure/; or keep them until the durable deployment exists. (D6) Whether the structural refactors (admission helpers, lane state module, core.ts split, verify split) run before or after the jam's move. The review recommends after, since they touch sealing transactions. These decisions are also recorded in notes/2026-10-02-simplification-review.md."}